# Cursor Rules for Echoing Sculk Sensors Minecraft Mod

## Project Overview
This is a Minecraft Fabric mod that adds Echoing Sculk Sensors to the game. The mod follows Fabric's architecture and conventions.

## Versions
- Use Java/Minecraft/Fabric/Fabric API version based on `gradle.properties` file

## Mod behaviour
- This mods adds a need item called "Echoing Sculk Sensor"
- It is crafted using a Sculk Sensor and 3 echo shards
- After it is placed it will listen for any sound vibrations (same rane as clibrated sculk sensors)
- It will remember the first sound it hears and will emit a redstone signal when it hears it again
- Once it has a stored sound it will only react ot that one specific sound
- Right clicking the sensor will clear the stored sound
- Powering the sensor will clear the stored sound as well (only one side, same is calibrated sculk sensors)
- For now it should use same texture as calibrated sculk sensors
- It can be water logged
- Same as sculk sensors, there is a 1 second cooldown period after being placed or after reseting the sound
- Same as Sculk sensors, Echoing Sculk sensors emit a redstone signal when they are activated when hearing the stored sound again.
    - The strength of the redstone signal is inversely proportional to the distance the vibration signal traveled
    - The closer the vibration is to the sculk sensor, the stronger the redstone signal is
- When measured with comporator, the redstone signal strength depends on the type of stored sound
    - Unlike sculk sensors, this can be measure at any point when a sound is stored, not only when the sound is heard

## Changing code
- Prefer using editor filesystem instead of command lines
- When making changes to code makes sure to delete imports that are no longer used
- Avoid changes to depedency versions defined in `gradle.properties` file
- When you need to run more complex scripts and powershell is not enough, prefer using Node.js over Python

